opriate you can send an email to our  support team  and we will help you choose the correct  code  as we mentioned earlier we do offer some  more general  high level codes for cases where the  precise diagnosis is unknown  for example in the case of a myeloid  disorder you know sometimes the  specific diagnosis is unknown early on  you could submit a case with a code for  myeloid neoplasm  and in that case we would return  information for the most common  disorders such as aml  mds and mpn  great thank you dr call our next  question is there a specific  list of diagnoses that we select from  when submitting a case to precision  insights  and as a follow-up question to that what  happens if we have a case with a  diagnosis that is  not on the precision precision insights  list  sure i can take that one as well um we  we do provide an  updated list of snomed light codes um  monthly to our clients um so you would  have a list  from which to choose when you were  submitting a case to us  um and for the follow-up um if if you  don't see  a diagnosis code on the list you would  reach out to our support team  and we will find and provide the most  appropriate code  based on the information that you give  and then  we would map that within our system in  time for you to submit your case  and then that would be included on the  updated list the next month  as an addition to our system  thank you so much dr call if a drug is  approved in a different disease  would we see it on the report  so i can take that question um yes you  would see it  um but as i showed you the um  the the diseases in the summary section  are shown as either approved in this  disease or approved in this indication  or we do also show  uh drugs that are approved in other  indications and  the each of them is shown with a level  of evidence so you can understand  if it's a level c point one that the  drug is approved  for that specific biomarker in a  different disease  versus a c point two or a level d where  there  it's a criteria for a clinical trial or  there's preclinical evidence for the use  of that drug  but yes we do include drugs that are  both approved on indication and  authentication thank you dr elkin  can you select clinical trials and qci  excuse me qci precision insights based  on the patient's location  and the second part is where do the  trials come from and how often is that  information updated  i can go ahead and take that one um the  patient location can be indicated  by either patient state or physician zip  code  and that information would be submitted  with the case  via the xml and trials  we find our trials primarily on  clinicaltrials.gov  and the who sites and we can also bring  in trials from other databases  and private sources as well as far as  updating um the clinicaltrials.gov  trials are updated on a nightly basis  in our system and the w80 trials are  updated on a regular basis but  less frequent than nightly  thank you dr call and i want to remind  our audience you know we are getting  some  amazing questions coming in any  questions that we don't have time for  today  will be answered via the contact  information that you provided at the  time of registration so please feel free  to keep these questions coming in  moving on to our next one what kind of  variants  can qci precision insights process and  interpret  and what data files can be uploaded  i can take that question so mo qci  precision insights can interpret  basically any kind of molecular result  that you can submit  um we can take any kind of ngs variance  so  single nucleotide variance small indels  structural variants fusions  rearrangements  copy number variants we can also take  cytogenetic variants and  fish we'll at ihc we'll work with our  clients to  ensure that we're using a consistent  controlled vocabulary so that we're  certain that for variants that aren't  described by  hgvs that we are  in agreement on the nomenclature for the  communication  of those variants in terms of what kinds  of data files can be uploaded  we work with our clients to define an  xml input so we work with you to take  your vcf or your  your your data file and submit it to us  in a standardized xml input  so that with allowing us to be able to  take not only  dna sequencing results but also the as i  mentioned the cytogenetic or fish or ihc  results as well  in addition to the diagnosis of the  patient  and the demographic information the age  and  gender that would also be used to  to filter the clinical trials  thank you dr elkin our next question  how long does it take for the  professional interpretation  service to provide me with inter  interpretive  comments  i can go ahead and take this one um we  we do have a fully automated service  that returns reports within minutes  which will contract for certain panels  and we also have an on-demand curation  service where turnaround time varies  based on the panel  and the disease the longest contracted  turnaround time would be up to three  business days  but some reports would still be returned  within minutes  and on average our turnaround time for  the curation service  is about a half a day on average  overall thank you dr call  so we have time for a few more questions  how are the oncologists involved in the  process  validating the clinical evidence in the  interpretation  summaries so  we have a fantastic team of oncologists  that have been working with us for a  very long time  um and over the years we've um made that  process more and more  um streamlined so um  we have they the oncologists review each  of the individual annotations  that refer to clinical evidence or um  any kind of clinical information  um and also answer any additional  questions  that our curators have our scientists  have in the process of their research  so they are working with us on a daily  basis we  um we have an automated system to alert  them when  um there are annotations ready for their  review  and we also reach out to them ad hoc to  get their clinical input  on the information that we're providing  thank you dr elkin and it looks like  we've got time for one more question  is it possible to configure the final  report  so yes our report outputs  are can be available either by xml or by  pdf  the pdf is a standardized pdf  um that you would be able to attach to  your report  um as an as an appendix or an edition  um and we're able to do things like  change the logo  and but not there's not a lot of  configuration available with that  particular pdf  however we also provide the information  by xml  and in the xml version  you would be able to parse that  information in whatever way  you wanted to do so that  you know you can use whatever pieces of  information from the xml  and display them in a way that that you  can customize yourself to  to you know preserve a brand or  or make your reports unique kaijen does  also have report services that can help  with  with reporting if if necessary  thank you again dr elkin and dr kaul for  your time today  and for your important research we would  also like to thank labberts and our  sponsor kayajin  for underwriting today's educational  webcast  before we go i'd like to thank the  audience for joining us today and for  their interesting questions  questions that we did not have time for  today and those submitted during the  on-demand period will be addressed by  our speakers via the contact information  that you provided at the time of  registration  this webcast can be viewed on demand  labyrints will alert you via email when  it's available for replay  we encourage you to share that email  with your colleagues who may have missed  today's live event  until next time thank you for joining us  bye-bye everyone
 

